# rusers (rpc.rusersd) configuration template
# This package provides NO_CONFIG_FILE as per schema.
# The rusers service is a legacy RPC-based service (portmapper/rpcinfo)
# that broadcasts user login information over the network.
# It is largely deprecated in modern Linux distributions in favor of
# systemd-logind and more secure monitoring solutions.
# If a configuration file exists in the target OS (e.g. /etc/rusersd.conf),
# it is typically empty or handled via command-line flags passed to the service.

# No configuration directives to render.
# To disable the service (recommended):
# ensure the service unit is masked or stopped.
# Example Ansible task:
# - name: Disable rusersd
#   ansible.builtin.service:
#     name: rpc-rusersd
#     enabled: false
#     state: stopped
#     masked: true